WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.730
In Rogue One: A Star Wars Story, virtually
every main character is killed during the

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:09.640
film's climax… but in the original version,
though, Jyn Erso and Cassian Andor actually

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:10.140
survive.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.220
How would the events of the original Star
Wars trilogy have been different if these

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.660
two heroes made it out alive?

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.900
Jyn Erso was the main protagonist of Rogue
One.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.980
She included elements of Luke Skywalker, Princess
Leia and Han Solo all rolled into her personality,

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:29.040
and would've fit right in with all of them
in the Rebellion's inner circle if she'd survived.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.420
She effectively leads the mission to steal
the Death Star plans, and shows off clever

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:38.510
planning skills, bravery, and leadership abilities
that could certainly come in handy during

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:42.220
the hard years that would follow the Battle
of Scarif… if she'd survived.

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:47.420
From the escape from the Death Star to the
frozen battlefields of Hoth, it's tough to

00:00:47.429 --> 00:00:51.100
imagine a battle in which Jyn wouldn't be
an asset.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:55.570
You also have to wonder if she could've found
herself as part of a love triangle with Princess

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:57.340
Leia and a smitten Han Solo.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:02.070
If she had, would there have ever been a Kylo
Ren to cause all that trouble in The Force

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:02.560
Awakens?

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:08.260
We meet Cassian Andor well into his career
as a spy, and from his very first moments,

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:12.200
it's clear he handles the uglier side of the
hope-filled Rebellion.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.060
"Calm down, it'll be all right,"

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:25.540
We've never really met a character like him
before in the big-screen Star Wars films,

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.900
so it would've been interesting to see the
contributions this kind of pragmatist might've

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.400
made in the war rooms of the original trilogy.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:37.299
He would've almost certainly brought a darker
edge to the Rebellion's tactics, and you have

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:42.140
to wonder what other useful intel he might
have acquired had he survived to keep fighting.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:47.660
While Erso and Andor were the only two heroes
to survive Rogue One's original screenplay,

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:51.840
how would the Star Wars universe have changed
if other important characters survived?

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:57.640
Lucasfilm has been open about the fact that
Saw Gerrera's role in Rogue One was originally

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:00.920
planned to be a whole lot more than what made
it to the screen.

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:05.980
After Saw was first introduced in the Clone
Wars animated series, Lucasfilm had bigger

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:09.200
plans for his team of extremist Rebels in
Rogue One.

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:14.220
Unfortunately, reshoots and edits led to much
of his planned story being left on the cutting

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:14.820
room floor.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:20.680
Instead, Gerrera's time on screen ended with
a bang pretty early in the film, as he's blown

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:23.080
up during the Death Star's first test shot.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:28.140
If he had lived, though, you have to wonder
what influence his guerilla tactics and extreme,

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.700
battle-scarred views might've had on the Rebellion
at large.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:36.080
The Rebels are desperate enough to seek him
out in Rogue One, so it stands to reason that

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:39.340
he could've risen to a leadership role under
the right circumstances.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:44.020
That might've given the Alliance some inner
turmoil from a faction that believed blowing

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:48.420
up the Death Star and throwing the Emperor
down a reactor shaft weren't going far enough

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:50.120
in getting vengeance on their enemies.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:55.020
We've seen plenty of splinter factions in
the Empire, including the First Order, but

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:59.360
if he'd lived, Saw Gerrera might've been the
one to push the good guys into a much darker

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:00.160
place, too.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:05.460
Chirrut Imwe and Baze Malbus were put out
of work when the Empire laid siege to the

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:09.890
ancient temple they'd been tasked with defending,
but they never lost their sense of what was

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:10.800
worth fighting for.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:16.140
As a result, they get roped into Jyn's mission,
and prove to be critically important soldiers

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:16.840
in the field.

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:21.200
They may not be Jedi, but they still fight
for the Force, and in Chirrut's case, that

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.500
dedication seems pretty unique.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:28.640
"The Force is with me, and I am with the Force,
and I fear nothing."

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:33.820
If these two had survived to the era of the
original trilogy, they could've combined that

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:37.650
same ground level approach with the renown
and respect they would've earned with their

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.520
crucial part in taking down the Empire's super-weapon.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:45.110
Maybe instead of the altruistic "May the Force
be with you," the Rebels would've been quoting

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:48.900
Chirrut's much more confident mantra, "the
Force is with me" instead.

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:54.570
Bodhi is instrumental in getting word out
that a flaw potentially exists in the Death

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:58.780
Star, after being given his secret mission
by Jyn's father from deep inside the Empire.

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:04.700
As far as his place in Rogue One, Bodhi serves
as the team's pilot and communications expert.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:09.320
He also shows some creativity in confusing
the Imperial soldiers by faking calls on the

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:13.720
radio to make it seem like their small strike
team is more like a full-on army.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:19.380
Had Bodhi survived, his outside the box approach
and ingenuity could've been more than useful

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:20.940
for the burgeoning Rebellion.

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:26.600
Up until Rogue One, we didn't really know
that anyone other than Grand Moff Tarkin was

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:30.180
in charge of the Death Star, but it all started
with Orson Krennic.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:35.640
This Imperial middle manager spends the entire
film trying to prove his worth to Tarkin,

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:40.040
Darth Vader and the rest of the Empire only
to get fragged alongside everyone else when

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:42.500
the Death Star gets its shot on Scarif.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:47.099
Could Krennic have been able to protect his
planet-killer when others failed?

00:04:47.099 --> 00:04:51.979
Well, if he had lived, you have to think Krennic's
ruthless ambition would've made him an even

00:04:51.979 --> 00:04:56.400
more brutal commander of the Death Star, and
his brush with death might've given him the

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.020
survival instinct that Grand Moff Tarkin lacked.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:04:59.940
"Evacuate?

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.720
In our moment of triumph?"

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:06.760
Galen's survival could've arguably had one
of the biggest butterfly effects on the Star

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:07.980
Wars universe at large.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:13.550
As the man who designed the Death Star, having
him survive to join the Rebels would've done

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:15.800
a lot more than just give Jyn her father back.

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:17.640
He would've been a game-changer.

00:05:18.189 --> 00:05:22.240
Not only does he know the Death Star inside
and out, but he would've also brought a great

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:26.219
scientific mind to the Rebellion and additional
knowledge on other Empire projects.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.139
He could've given the Rebels the edge, and
tipped the scales in the war while a certain

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:34.760
famous farm boy was still bullseyeing Womp-Rats
in his T-16 back home on Tatooine.

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:41.039
Despite the fact that he doesn't seem to have
much regard for organic beings, K-2SO heroically

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:46.139
sacrifices his life to buy Jyn and Cassian
enough time to liberate the Death Star plans.

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:50.400
Had he survived the film, you could absolutely
imagine him hanging out and providing some

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.880
snarky comic relief throughout the original
trilogy.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:59.520
Imagine a Star Wars universe where this hulking,
combat-ready droid replaced C-3PO as R2-D2's

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:00.180
best buddy.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:04.320
Put those two together, and we could wrap
up A New Hope in about 45 minutes.

